About the Staff Product Manager Role at QuintoAndar

Our product management team is built on a two-sided career path consisting of a managerial track and an individual contributor track. Both tracks provide equal growth potential and seniority levels. A Staff PM is a seasoned professional acting as an individual contributor that has gone beyond the Sr. PM role. You will be tackling some of the toughest challenges we have along a senior team of designers and engineers.

&nbsp;

Staff Product Manager responsibilities at QuintoAndar:

• Lead a senior product squad, prioritizing its bets, and coordinating cross initiatives.

• Influence business strategy and product organization. Help the business to scale fast and enable a sustainable growth;

• Lead OKRs planning and quarterly roadmap for the squad. We expect you to drive strategy, and ensure the execution flowing as planned;

• Ensure your squad is well organized, productive, and happy. Iterate rituals and integrate product, operations, design, engineering, data, and QA.

• Deep dive into execution, grab different inputs and discuss the end-game solution with key stakeholders. Set expectations and help the team translate complex problems into product vision and roadmap;

• Kick-off new discovery streams, anticipate pilots, and validate hypotheses before the quarterly planning. Ensure we are using engineering wisely;

• Study big trends that affect your product. Ensure you are bringing insights from outside world and connecting dots.

• Coach APMs. Give training and invest in people development;

• Play a key role in the PM hiring process and help us to scale an A player team.

&nbsp;

Requirements:

• Please only apply if you fulfill these:

• Product track record: you already proved you are a great Product Manager, delivering high-impact solutions.

• Leadership skills: you have worked a few yeas in leadership positions, successfully managing cross-functional teams;

• Hard skills: you are very analytical and tuned into industry benchmarks to solve our client's needs. We are looking for exceptional problem solvers;

• Design thinking: demonstrated ability to gather user requirements (even when the user does not know about it) and convert them into a compelling product vision;

• Fast-pace: you are used to aggressive launch dates and make decisions in a fast-changing environment.

